{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/1500113-travel-times-on-the-midnight-express","id":1500113,"title":"Travel Times on the Midnight Express","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-12-19T11:39:47-08:00","id":1500113,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Travel Times on the Midnight Express","content":"So, I've been looking into the Midnight Express, but I can't seem to find an explanation on travel times. The only example of a timeline I could find was on Xenophon's fake train.<br /> <br /> How is the travel time determined? And does the train arrive at the car's destination at midnight of the next night, or the same night (depending on time zones?)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26895-bastardquest","name":"bastardquest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26895_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-19T12:35:06-08:00","id":1500118,"title":"","content":"My understanding is that it always arrives exactly at midnight and always departs at exactly 12:03 AM at every stop in its time zone. So the travel time is always dependent on what time zone the passengers want to go to.<br /> <br /> So if the passenger boards in New York City necropolis's station and wants to get off at the Chicago station (which is in the next time zone), the passenger will only need to travel for one hour. If the passenger wants to depart in the Los Angeles station, it'd be three hours later. If the passenger wants to depart at London, it'd be nineteen hours. If the passenger wanted to depart at a station somewhere else in the Eastern Time Zone (say Boston, Toronto, Miami, Havana, or Lima) then it'd be 24 hours.<br /> <br /> This is a magical train that appears in multiple places at the same moment in time so there is a lot of weirdness. It also means that the Midnight Express won't be the best option if you can get to your destination by another means quicker. Someone travelling from New York to Boston might have better options (a relic car with enough Pathos fuel, a cart pulled by moliated wraiths, another relic train that travels only in the Shadowlands without the special powers of the Express, etc.) than waiting a full 24 hours for the Midnight Express to arrive. But for many wraiths it'll be a fast and safe option.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}